course: biology
lesson: 135
title: Kung Fu Panda: real giant pandas and red pandas
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Po loves dumplings and noodles, but a real giant panda spends about half of every day munching bamboo, the only food it really needs.
explain: A panda is a true bear with a meat-eater's gut, so it gets little goodness from bamboo and must eat a huge amount and rest a lot to save energy.
explain: Watch a panda eat and you will see it hold a bamboo stalk like you hold a carrot: an enlarged wrist bone works like an extra thumb.
explain: Master Shifu is a red panda, a real animal but not a close cousin of the giant panda; it was called panda first, and the giant panda was named after it.
fact: Real giant pandas eat almost only bamboo, about 12 to 38 kilograms a day, and spend about 12 to 14 hours a day eating.
fact: Bamboo has little goodness, so pandas must eat a lot and rest to save energy.
fact: Pandas have an enlarged wrist bone that works like a thumb to grip bamboo, often called the panda's thumb, though it is not a true thumb.
fact: Giant pandas are bears with a meat-eater's gut, so they digest bamboo poorly, and they sometimes eat meat such as small animals when they find it.
fact: Young pandas really tumble and roll, and pandas are good climbers that can rest high in tree branches.
fact: A newborn panda weighs about 100 grams, about a bar of chocolate, while its mother is around 900 times heavier; cubs are born pink and blind, and the black and white fur grows in after a few weeks.
fact: Wild giant pandas live in cool, damp mountain bamboo forests in central China, and they do not hibernate because bamboo can be found all winter.
fact: Scientists think panda colours help them hide in snow and shade, while black ears and eye patches may send signals; each panda's eye patches are a slightly different shape.
fact: Red pandas have their own family; they also eat bamboo and have a thumb-like wrist bone, but they evolved it separately from giant pandas.
fact: Red pandas live in cold mountain forests, wrap their thick tail around themselves like a blanket and have fur on the soles of their feet for icy branches.
fact: Giant pandas were moved from endangered to vulnerable in 2016 after their numbers rose, thanks to protected forests and bamboo corridors; about 1,800 live in the wild.
fact: Snow leopards, like Tai Lung, live in high mountains of Asia, with thick fur, wide paws that work like snowshoes and a long tail for balance; they cannot roar.
exercise: What does a real giant panda eat almost all the time? | Bamboo | Dumplings and noodles | Raw fish | Fruit and honey
exercise: About how many hours a day does a panda spend eating? | About 12 to 14 | About 1 | About 24 | About 3
exercise: Why must a panda eat so much bamboo? | Bamboo has little goodness in it | Bamboo makes pandas grow taller | Pandas store bamboo for winter | Pandas eat to keep their teeth short
exercise: What helps a panda grip a bamboo stalk? | An enlarged wrist bone that works like a thumb | Sticky pads on its paws like a gecko's feet | A long gripping tail | Long claws that bend and grip like human fingers
exercise: Is the panda's thumb a true thumb? | No, it is an enlarged wrist bone | Yes, just like a person's thumb | Yes, it is a sixth finger with a nail | No, it is a piece of bamboo
exercise: What kind of animal is a giant panda? | A bear | A kind of raccoon | A kind of cat | A big red panda
exercise: Can pandas climb trees? | Yes, they are good climbers and may rest in branches | No, they are far too heavy and their claws are too blunt | Only in the film | Only when they are newborn
exercise: About how much does a newborn panda weigh? | About 100 grams, like a bar of chocolate | About 10 kilograms, as heavy as a middle-sized dog | About 1 gram, like a paper clip | About 50 kilograms, like a person
exercise: What colour is a newborn panda? | Pink, and it is blind | Black and white like its mother | All black | Bright orange
exercise: Where do wild giant pandas live? | In mountain bamboo forests of central China | In the hot, wet jungles of central and western Africa | On the ice of the Arctic | In the deserts of Australia
exercise: Why do pandas not hibernate? | Bamboo can be found all winter | They are too thin to sleep | They live where there is no winter | They sleep all summer instead
exercise: What may a panda's black and white colours do? | Help it hide in snow and shade and send signals | Scare away tigers and wolves that come too close | Keep its skin cool in the desert | Show which pandas are boys
exercise: Is a red panda a close relative of the giant panda? | No, it has its own family | Yes, it is a baby giant panda | Yes, it is a giant panda that turned red | No, it is a kind of small fox
exercise: Which animal was called panda first? | The red panda | The giant panda | The snow leopard | The common raccoon
exercise: How does a red panda keep warm? | Wraps its thick tail around itself and has furry feet | Sleeps in the warm water of hot springs all through the winter | Shivers all night long | Grows feathers in winter
exercise: Why were giant pandas moved from endangered to vulnerable in 2016? | Their numbers rose after forests were protected | They were all moved to zoos, so none of them were in danger any more | Their numbers fell to zero | They learned to eat meat
exercise: What kind of real animal is Tai Lung? | A snow leopard | A tiger | A lion | A cheetah
exercise: What do a snow leopard's wide paws do? | Work like snowshoes | Help it swim fast in rivers | Dig up young bamboo shoots | Make its roar sound louder
test: «2 pandas eating bamboo, how many of those fake thumbs, one per front paw» | 4 | 2 | 8 | 1
test: «Po lives on noodles n dumplings so pandas eat anything» What is right? | Real pandas eat almost only bamboo, sometimes a little meat | Yes, pandas love noodles in the wild and steal them from farms | Yes, they hunt for dumplings | No, pandas eat only fish
test: «baby panda's a mini black and white bear from day one» What is right? | Cubs are born pink and blind, and the black and white fur grows in later | Yes, they are born fully black and white, with their eyes wide open from the start | No, they are born all black | No, they are born orange like red pandas
test: «Shifu's a red panda so he's a baby panda innit» What is right? | No, red pandas are a separate family of their own | Yes, red pandas grow up into giant pandas when they are older | Yes, they are the same animal in red | No, red pandas are a kind of bear
test: In Winnie the Pooh, a bear lives on honey. What does the real giant panda live on? | Bamboo | Wild honey | River salmon | Berries and fish
test: «panda spent all day eating then sleeping, lazy git» Why does it really do that? | Bamboo has little goodness, so it must eat a lot and rest to save energy | It is just bored, as there is nothing else to do all day in a bamboo forest | It is hibernating | It is ill
test: What would happen to a panda if all the bamboo in its forest died? | It would go hungry, as bamboo is almost all it eats | It would switch to noodles and rice from the nearest farm at once | It would hibernate until spring | Nothing, it eats mostly meat
test: «Tai Lung roars like a lion in the film so snow leopards roar» What is right? | Snow leopards cannot roar | Yes, they roar louder than lions | Yes, but only in snow | No, they bark like dogs
test: «why does nobody worry about pandas anymore» What is right? | Their numbers rose with protected forests, but about 1,800 are still in the wild | Pandas are now everywhere in China, even in the cities, so they need no more help at all | Pandas no longer exist in the wild | Pandas only live in zoos now
test: «pandas sleep all winter like other bears, right» What is right? | No, they stay awake because bamboo can be found all winter | Yes, they sleep in deep dens from October right through to April | Yes, in caves under the snow | No, they sleep all summer
test: «red pandas have bare feet like dogs» What is right? | They have fur on the soles of their feet for icy branches | Yes, completely bare and rough, just like the pads on a dog's paws | They have hooves | They have webbed feet
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning the diet of the giant panda. | It consists almost exclusively of bamboo, supplemented occasionally by small animals | It consists principally of cooked cereals and dumplings, as is depicted in the animated film | It consists exclusively of fish taken from mountain streams | It consists principally of fruit and honey
exam: Identify the anatomical structure by means of which the giant panda grasps the stalks of bamboo. | An enlarged bone of the wrist which functions in the manner of a thumb | A true opposable thumb identical to that of the human hand | A prehensile tail employed as a fifth limb | Adhesive pads upon the soles of the feet
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the relationship between the red panda and the giant panda? | The red panda belongs to a separate family and is not a close relative of the giant panda | The red panda is the juvenile form of the giant panda, its coat darkening to black and white with age | The red panda is a giant panda of reddish colouring | The red panda is a member of the bear family
exam: Ascertain the reason for which the giant panda does not hibernate. | Its food, bamboo, remains available throughout the winter | It is incapable of accumulating any reserve of fat | Its habitat experiences no winter season | It hibernates during the summer months instead
